#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059462 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73ad4cd2-e7f0-5b7d-82fc-1a8e4b0597d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of the Hypotenuse of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Legs"}] :question/id #uuid "d1277863-7d33-566d-91b9-7a78458dca8e" :question/math-academy-id "e-3077" :question/problem "If the side that is opposite to a $45^\\circ$ angle in an isosceles right triangle has a length of $3,$ what is the length of the hypotenuse?\n\n![](images/11/11036dee7004fef1c43977a8a80bb46d4277834e558ac926b851d3fd5639965b.png)" :question/worked-solution "The hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are the sides that are opposite the $45^\\circ$ angles. So in the given triangle, the legs have length $3.$\n\nConsequently, the hypotenuse has a length of\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2} \\cdot 3 = 3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059463 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5faa905-dcfc-5eed-b4ed-5818ca6ef342" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of the Legs of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Hypotenuse"}] :question/id #uuid "ce112319-10a9-5483-82c3-566c0630b23a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3080" :question/problem "If the hypotenuse of a $45^\\circ$-$45^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle has a length of $5,$ then what is the length of each leg?" :question/worked-solution "The hypotenuse in a $45^\\circ$-$45^\\circ$-$90^\\circ$ triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nHere, we know that the hypotenuse has length $5.$ So, if the length of a leg is $a,$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot a \\\\ a & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the square root from the denominator, we can multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{5\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\ a & =\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $\\dfrac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059464 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ae8076e-25bc-5489-ae14-ffa16d17a32c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of the Diagonal or Side of a Square Given its Perimeter"}] :question/id #uuid "0d244991-c12e-5c56-8f58-762d8be22f8a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3082" :question/problem "Find the length of the diagonal $\\overline{AC}$ of the square $ABCD$ if the perimeter of the square is $p=256\\,\\mathrm{mm}.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the perimeter is $p=256\\,\\textrm{mm},$ the length of a single side is\n\n$$\nAB = \\dfrac{p}{4} = \\dfrac{256}{4} = 64\\,\\mathrm{mm}.\n$$\n\nNow, consider $\\triangle{ABC}$, which is an isosceles right triangle since $\\angle{ABC} = 90^\\circ$ and $AB=BC.$\n\n![](images/5b/5bb28a161b88919351ee8e83c2943817f20c124d80fb24c4ceffe29129fbbb07.png)\n\nThe hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nHere, the length of a leg is $AB=64,$ so the length of the hypotenuse is\n\n$$\nAC = \\sqrt{2}\\cdot AB = \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 64 = 64\\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{mm}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the diagonal of the square $ABCD$ has a length of $AC= 64 \\sqrt{2} \\, \\textrm{mm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059466 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16fd63e8-664f-53c2-b623-c696b86b5642" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Hypotenuse or Leg of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given its Perimeter"}] :question/id #uuid "e4466ef9-61d2-5b02-960b-c5c421a9dc1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3085" :question/problem "The perimeter of the triangle below is $26+13\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of the hypotenuse.\n\n![](images/d1/d194f2c2ce34bd40f5da5dd9e30048a6cc9318a1308c8a7e5d7156cb58a76134.png)" :question/worked-solution "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC = AB\\cdot\\sqrt{2} = a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p = 26+13\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 26+13\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 26+13\\sqrt{2} & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 13(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =a(2+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 13\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =a\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\ 13 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $a=13,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is\n\n$$\nAC = a \\sqrt{2} = 13 \\sqrt{2} .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16fd63e8-664f-53c2-b623-c696b86b5642" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Hypotenuse or Leg of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given its Perimeter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2da781e7-de87-52ec-b185-094fd978c03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496758} {:answer/id #uuid "84438ce6-8742-54c4-aa8e-51fad463771e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496928} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e72d65-6ad1-567b-af37-eadf981e3d7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497067} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf121f1-43b2-5c24-b9f8-c8d50bd203a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497203} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6e0d92-1f64-5d70-b3fa-256c0ec1858b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2da781e7-de87-52ec-b185-094fd978c03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496758} :answer-field/id #uuid "0586ffd3-605c-5a29-9f28-b17f58181dec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497210}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b09b9f2c-ef1d-5c6b-ab4f-39e0069d6d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-119321" :question/problem "![](images/70/70d961102240b0c48132baca8db0b77ed80ff8e0d3b7296bd5c727ab2f97dfd3.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $18+9\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg." :question/worked-solution "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=18+9\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 18+9\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 9(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 9(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 9\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 9 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5faa905-dcfc-5eed-b4ed-5818ca6ef342" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of the Legs of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Hypotenuse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48443432-020a-5120-9c81-c064952d24fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496821} {:answer/id #uuid "b02218e1-b40a-52ee-b27c-7a9dac34a242" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497014} {:answer/id #uuid "b1147b51-98f8-5c9e-9729-82607e5c702b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497019} {:answer/id #uuid "e01ad27a-bc50-5bbb-b521-a3e2f6c464f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497138} {:answer/id #uuid "e1592bd0-f210-50d4-8bd5-03e1e35596fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e01ad27a-bc50-5bbb-b521-a3e2f6c464f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497138} :answer-field/id #uuid "873745d1-6a16-5919-9ae3-c4d7910f9a77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0fe06fc-b588-5b7a-af64-41bd4d958847" :question/math-academy-id "q-1661" :question/problem "If the hypotenuse of a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle has a length of $9$, then what is the length of each leg?" :question/worked-solution "The hypotenuse in a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nHere, we know that the hypotenuse has length $9.$ So, if the length of a leg is $a,$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot a \\\\ a & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the square root from the denominator, we can multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{9\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497406 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ae8076e-25bc-5489-ae14-ffa16d17a32c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of the Diagonal or Side of a Square Given its Perimeter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18e75242-8fa3-5f94-a933-6b370faaf7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496710} {:answer/id #uuid "83e5621e-4a8e-57c7-8309-681975e016b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496927} {:answer/id #uuid "b43f80eb-55aa-597a-9275-556c6157c0c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "384\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497027} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1b0cb8-96c0-5290-8143-a09417c291eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "195\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497048} {:answer/id #uuid "ddf96216-6dc0-5f6c-8d56-97e03f44a4f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192\\sqrt{2}\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18e75242-8fa3-5f94-a933-6b370faaf7ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496710} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e80948-aa5c-55f7-a72e-e8c26ffe9e91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dec9b8fc-0644-5c4f-9a1c-3c1062dcc187" :question/math-academy-id "q-20303" :question/problem "Find the perimeter of a square whose diagonal is $\\frac{48}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,mm.$" :question/worked-solution "A diagram of the given situation is shown below.\n\n![](images/58/5844e63004f2c12f7af15b2fe178a3e48f67e63d06692db532e5261d3f9f7df6.png)\n\nNotice that $△FHG$ is a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle since $HG=GF$ and $m∠HGF={90}^{∘}.$\n\nThe hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. \n\nHere, the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{FH}$ is $\\frac{48}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,mm.$ So the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{HG}$ can be found by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FH & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot HG \\\\ \\frac{48}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot HG \\\\ HG & =\\frac{48}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\ HG & =\\frac{48}{2} \\\\ HG & =24\\,mm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the perimeter $p$ is given by\n\n$$\np=4\\cdot HG=4\\cdot 24=96\\,mm.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059638 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16fd63e8-664f-53c2-b623-c696b86b5642" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of a Hypotenuse or Leg of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given its Perimeter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe8010f-1547-5782-9bee-cf63beb39dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496690} {:answer/id #uuid "228610ed-b7ea-5588-9f8f-f46d388b1b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496730} {:answer/id #uuid "3d863720-9933-5260-827e-e7dcada92695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496792} {:answer/id #uuid "9449aa6a-9cf8-5648-9f77-f4d5a80d65cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496966} {:answer/id #uuid "ff9434b1-21e8-55f6-ac9d-22292feaee4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d863720-9933-5260-827e-e7dcada92695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496792} :answer-field/id #uuid "05afe7d8-ea5f-55da-9dc3-859108f0ebfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f843f904-8144-53f3-a620-84dc239149a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-22025" :question/problem "![](images/10/1073020fe8576784ed24601864f8546a72b426d8f02670b1a8c13923dc16e35f.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the triangle above is $16+8\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of the hypotenuse." :question/worked-solution "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=16+8\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 16+8\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 16+8\\sqrt{2} & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 8(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =a(2+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 8\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =a\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\ 8 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $a=8,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is\n\n$$\nAC=a\\sqrt{2}=8\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73ad4cd2-e7f0-5b7d-82fc-1a8e4b0597d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of the Hypotenuse of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Legs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2024a224-9857-5270-9cd7-d217a745fa8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496727} {:answer/id #uuid "abd0293b-b4ac-539a-8abc-db8c78a93f1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497007} {:answer/id #uuid "b59077d6-0ce5-5464-9d88-0b75f45070ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497031} {:answer/id #uuid "bfe7d01a-7b16-56b3-91e2-f666d9b3cca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497052} {:answer/id #uuid "fb5a6999-a960-53c0-b074-796027e04a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb5a6999-a960-53c0-b074-796027e04a89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497198} :answer-field/id #uuid "715ed1d3-fc1a-56d7-9722-4551ff9be14b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497272}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7f5740bd-61d8-5b2e-a862-8cfe4f8c625d" :question/math-academy-id "q-4346" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8eeeb4e409d681d34dcc4c4926e9da8c1759b96e6a28517d5ee2837d4d98f4ed.png)\n\nIf the side that is opposite to a ${45}^{∘}$ angle in an isosceles right triangle has a length of $4,$ what is the length of the hypotenuse?" :question/worked-solution "The hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are the sides that are opposite the ${45}^{∘}$ angles. So in the given triangle, the legs have length $4.$\n\nConsequently, the hypotenuse has a length of\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059630 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "73ad4cd2-e7f0-5b7d-82fc-1a8e4b0597d8" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of the Hypotenuse of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Legs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29554996-89a9-5ba8-8c88-e745c2edc7d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496748} {:answer/id #uuid "3989ccc3-4df8-51e2-8ae0-6a3f4e565699" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496782} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd2c703-8743-5512-ba7e-a6182dc0dada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496951} {:answer/id #uuid "b1732fcf-1a03-5c0e-a435-6656d6201cef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497021} {:answer/id #uuid "c9337c7d-f316-5bd2-8e8d-de7d4e0ff7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bd2c703-8743-5512-ba7e-a6182dc0dada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496951} :answer-field/id #uuid "063290b7-eb1e-5cfd-a98b-55f38d184348" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6079d028-93a0-532f-b302-a8dd0dd1bda6" :question/math-academy-id "q-53405" :question/problem "![](images/83/83500660f574c604d0cd1bab3849bf252de7d8e98bd7da2bb163c6178ad7383a.png)\n\nIf the side that is opposite to a ${45}^{∘}$ angle in an isosceles right triangle has a length of $\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{2}},$ what is the length of the hypotenuse?" :question/worked-solution "The hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are the sides that are opposite the ${45}^{∘}$ angles. So in the given triangle, the legs have length $\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{2}}.$\n\nConsequently, the hypotenuse has a length of\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{12}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{12\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}=12.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059631 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5faa905-dcfc-5eed-b4ed-5818ca6ef342" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Length of the Legs of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Hypotenuse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2834fefa-7f82-5f0b-8bd4-2d77d0484f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496744} {:answer/id #uuid "89dd33bf-ff23-574f-a33b-5272aaa9a18c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496947} {:answer/id #uuid "9c69b0a7-2b7f-5a66-8d3d-4b86f69b1185" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496986} {:answer/id #uuid "aaafbf9f-f8a0-56af-b633-a2e30f2c2c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497005} {:answer/id #uuid "de069671-bd7e-5ede-b13a-854ad022115b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89dd33bf-ff23-574f-a33b-5272aaa9a18c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496947} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6ad8446-f31c-5ee8-8714-f141bf606e42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "35801314-b041-51b6-a1e8-f30ce1df3daa" :question/math-academy-id "q-53421" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a789720bf1dca7c32369d21c2eb2760b0de5524b49a489358df88c97ac7c137a.png)\n\nWhat is the length of one leg of the triangle above?" :question/worked-solution "The hypotenuse in a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nHere, we know that the hypotenuse has length $8.$ So, if the length of a leg is $a,$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot a \\\\ a & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the square root from the denominator, we can multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{8\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $4\\sqrt{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ae8076e-25bc-5489-ae14-ffa16d17a32c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of the Diagonal or Side of a Square Given its Perimeter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "312e6b26-669b-53cc-bdaa-2d36e57baf0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{2}\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496764} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb754c5-cff4-51d3-97bb-fd8c66ae755e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sqrt{2}\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496795} {:answer/id #uuid "4e7fd649-6808-5e4f-8865-ffd3241cf71c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496831} {:answer/id #uuid "6904d546-e7c4-55b7-893a-7a2acec2debd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496888} {:answer/id #uuid "c6dae4ef-d386-5b1d-932c-2a143932922f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6dae4ef-d386-5b1d-932c-2a143932922f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\,mm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497066} :answer-field/id #uuid "de85ca85-cfca-5077-b001-eb09d4064c99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b98ef3ce-085e-5f9a-9275-e9406accdcee" :question/math-academy-id "q-82309" :question/problem "Find the perimeter of a square whose diagonal is $\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,mm.$" :question/worked-solution "A diagram of the given situation is shown below.\n\n![](images/62/62e30b7b3f72b70df25a16b2d3b48423692892df19c9a7fcf99ba2201bb9ce09.png)\n\nNotice that $△FHG$ is a ${45}^{∘}$-${45}^{∘}$-${90}^{∘}$ triangle since $HG=GF$ and $m∠HGF={90}^{∘}.$\n\nThe hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. \n\nHere, the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{FH}$ is $\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,mm.$ So the length of the leg $\\overset{―}{HG}$ can be found by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FH & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot HG \\\\ \\frac{10}{\\sqrt{2}} & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot HG \\\\ HG & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}} \\\\ HG & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ HG & =5\\,mm\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the perimeter $p$ is given by\n\n$$\np=4\\cdot HG=4\\cdot 5=20\\,mm.\n$$"}]}
